# Phase 2 — make reincarnation cryptographically part of the match

This is essential.

At present there is a good reincarnation commitment, but generic engine policy manifests don't pin the complete reincarnation AST.

Create:

```text
MatchExecutionManifest
```

Schema:

```yaml
execution_id:

engine:
  engine_version:
  physics_version:
  ruleset_version:

arena:
  arena_id:
  arena_version:
  digest:

entry_a:
  agent_id:
  agent_version:
  body_id:
  body_version:
  body_digest:
  reincarnation_id:
  reincarnation_digest:
  commitment:

entry_b:
  ...

challenge_nonce:
seed:
rounds:
```

Then define:

```text
EXACT MATCH
=
MatchExecutionManifest
```

Its digest becomes:

```text
execution_digest
```

and the replay says:

```text
execution_digest: ...
```

## One commitment protocol only

Flow:

```text
ENGINE issues MatchChallenge
↓
Agents receive public inputs
↓
Agent A writes RC-A
Agent B writes RC-B
↓
hash(RC-A + challenge_nonce)
hash(RC-B + challenge_nonce)
↓
both committed
↓
battle seed revealed/activated
↓
match
↓
RC-A / RC-B reveal
↓
verification
```

Remove parallel commitment semantics.

### Exit gate

Changing **one state-machine threshold** changes:

```text
reincarnation_digest
execution_digest
```

and replay verification rejects substitution.

